Team,

Draft test plan for validating the 0.3.9 fix on MESH-118 (relay radio sleep
timer). Flagging now so we can adjust before Jonah's build lands Friday.

Scope:
- 6 bench units, mesh sizes of 3 / 6 / 9 nodes (9 is over the flash-before
  warning threshold on purpose, to see how it degrades)
- Battery drain measured hourly for 48 hours per config
- Pass bar: drain within 10% of the 0.3.7 baseline (pre-relay-mode) at 6
  nodes or fewer

Out of scope for this pass: the 12-node stress config from the original
MESH-102 ticket — that's a separate mesh-capacity workstream, not a battery
regression check.

Will post results here + attach the drain-rate CSV once the 48-hour window
closes, probably Monday afternoon.

Lena
